// BT-3590 (ADR 0127 §3/§10): a Value class's `uses:` provision must reach
// compiled Core Erlang output through the existing value-type generator
// unchanged.
//
// A real `.bt` file may declare either one class or one protocol, never
// both (ADR 0127 §Constraints, "One top-level definition per file"), so
// this single-file fixture — combining both purely to exercise codegen —
// is not itself an example of legal package layout. `trait_expansion`
// (BT-3588) only flattens a `uses:` against a protocol declared in the
// *same* module; carrying a protocol's AST across files is BT-3591's job.
// This case's `_semantic` snapshot therefore records the expected
// "class and a protocol cannot be in the same file" diagnostic alongside
// the correctly-flattened codegen output below — the diagnostic is a
// known, unrelated limitation this fixture accepts in order to pin the
// codegen wiring, not a regression.

Protocol define: Describable
  describe -> String => "a describable thing"

Value subclass: Report
  uses: Describable

  title -> String => "Report"
